WEBVTT

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.320
I'm Taniyama Mai,

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:13.990
1st-Year high-schooler.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:18.330
I have kind of a weird job.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:21.330
Wow, what an amazing house!

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:25.120
That's Shibuya Kazuya there with me.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.960
He's my boss at work.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:45.020
I'm so sorry to have to drag
you out all this way.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:49.020
My sister-in-law, Kana,
and my niece, Ayami.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.820
My brother is on a business
trip overseas right now,

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:55.700
and it's just us in the house,
so I'm feeling uneasy.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:59.030
About three days ago, this woman,
Morishita Noriko-san,

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:03.370
came into the office where I work,
and hired us to do an investigation.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.380
There's something strange
about the house.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:10.040
The furniture will suddenly
start to rattle,

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:13.720
I'll hear knocking on the walls
of rooms, when no one is in them,

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:18.050
and doors that shouldn't be
open will open up on their own.

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:20.390
There's just a lot of strange
things happening.

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:23.060
Who is in charge here?

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.390
I am the manager, Shibuya Kazuya.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:28.400
You...

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.400
It's only natural that
she'd be surprised.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.070
After all, our manager
is still in his teens.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:36.740
He's always so full of himself,

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:40.740
so I've nicknamed him "Narcissistic
Naru-chan." So then...

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:45.750
Well, all right. Is this really
the work of, you know, ghosts?

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:49.080
It's our job to investigate that.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:52.420
The office that he manages is our own

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.090
"Shibuya Psychic Research."

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.190
When we do investigations,
we always set up a room

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.990
in the place we are investigating
that we call a "base."

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.870
This is the center from which
we look into all sorts of things.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:47.370
What is the equipment status
in each room?

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:50.200
Monitor connections are normal.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:54.380
- This is Lin-san, Naru's assistant.
He doesn't talk very much,
- Each room is operating normally.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.630
And is a bit scary, so I have
trouble dealing with him.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:00.840
I wonder if it couldn't
be a poltergeist.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.340
Going by what Noriko-san said...

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:08.220
Oh, you're starting to sound like
a grown-up there, part-timer.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:09.890
Monk!

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:10.890
Yo.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:13.900
This is Takigawa Hosho,
a former Koyasan monk.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:17.730
Overdoing things as usual, I see,
with this mountain of equipment.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:21.240
She's Matsuzaki Ayako,
a self-styled shrine priestess.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:24.070
Neither of these two
are members of SPR,

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:26.240
but they've come to help
us with any exorcisms.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:28.580
Let me see.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:31.250
I'd say this is the work
of an earth spirit or something.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:34.250
I think it's the work of humans.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:35.920
My, listen to you!

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:38.250
Now, now, just listen.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:42.260
Humans are the culprits in half
of all poltergeisting, right?

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:45.260
And many of them are cases
of women under stress.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:48.260
And if you're looking for any
likely women in this house,

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:50.470
it'd be someone who can't get
along with their sister-in-law.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:51.600
You mean Noriko-san?

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:56.600
Indeed. Kana-san does seem
a bit grating, huh?

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:57.940
Well-deduced.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:00.070
Amateurish, shallow thinking.

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:03.280
In cases of poltergeisting
where a human is the culprit,

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:07.280
it's usually a young teen-
an adolescent child.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:11.620
Noriko-san is 20, too grown-up
to be called an adolescent.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:15.290
- But...
- True, there are cases
of spiritually sensitive women.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:18.290
I will conduct an experiment
regarding that tonight.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.630
W-why, you...

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:23.630
Excuse me for having
such shallow thinking!

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:26.300
Why did I fall in with that guy,
of all people?

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.220
Mai-chan, perfect timing.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.970
It's time for Ayami's snack.
Care to tag along?

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.640
All right!

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:37.310
Ayami-chan is so cute, isn't she?

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:39.980
If you had to say, does she
take more after her father?

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:42.320
Mm-mm, her mother.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:45.320
But she doesn't look all
that much like Kana-san...

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:48.320
Oh, my sister-in-law
is my brother's second wife.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:51.330
Ayami is his previous
wife's daughter.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:52.660
I'm sorry...

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:54.330
Don't worry about it.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:06:00.000
Ayami? Snack time.
Mai-chan is here, too.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.090
Hello there! Can I come in?

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:09.590
How cute!

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:14.350
Hello.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:17.350
Hello. What's your name?

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:20.350
Minnie!

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:26.360
My, Ayami, were you reading that book?

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:30.360
What's wrong?

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:33.370
Come on, let's have a snack.

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:36.040
Ayami doesn't want it.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:40.370
What came over her so suddenly?

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.890
Please focus on the light.

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:00.390
Naru first did an experiment
to determine

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:04.230
if the culprit behind the
poltergeisting was human or not.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:08.740
Please match your
breathing to the light.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.740
Slowly now...

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:16.410
They say that in the case
of people doing it,

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:21.080
they unconsciously use some
kind of supernatural ability.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:25.420
So when a suggestion is planted
into the subconscious...

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:32.590
Tonight, a vase will move.
A small, glass vase.

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:36.760
It will be on the table
in this room tonight.

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:39.430
If the person who receives
the suggestion is the culprit,

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:42.100
they will do what Naru says.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:49.440
Very good. Please spend the rest
of the evening as you like.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:51.450
Morishita-san, could I have
the key to this room?

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.110
Y-yes...

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:00.450
The suggestion worked.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:04.130
Everyone's eyes being focused
on the vase was proof of that.

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:13.800
If the culprit of the poltergeisting
was human, the vase would move.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:18.470
If it doesn't move,
then the culprit isn't human.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:28.480
Any movement?

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:29.980
None.

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:36.820
Come, quickly!

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:45.500
I was coming to tuck Ayami-chan
into bed, when I saw this!

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:47.500
Everything is slanted!

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.170
What's going on?

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:53.340
I thought you came here
to get this under control!

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:56.220
You're sure the little girl
didn't do it, right?

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:01.520
There's no way she could have!

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:02.850
You're right.

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:06.190
The furniture is still on top of it.
Even I couldn't do it.

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:08.190
There aren't any signs of anything.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.610
If there were a human
who could do this,

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:12.690
I'd sure like to meet them.

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:14.320
I was just saying...

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:16.530
It wasn't Ayami.

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:18.700
Uh-huh, it sure wasn't.

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:21.700
Noriko-san!?

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:29.880
This time, everything was upside-down.

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:32.670
Even the carpet has been turned over!

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.220
That settles it, it's a poltergeist.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:36.550
The culprit is an earth spirit.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:39.220
I'll have it driven out
as early as tomorrow,

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:41.560
just you watch. Good night.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:43.430
Where does she get her confidence?

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:44.890
What's the matter?

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:47.060
You're thinking hard
about something, huh?

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:48.900
Is there something bothering you?

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:51.570
Don't you think this response
is a little quick?

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:54.900
Psychic phenomena tend
to have an aversion to outsiders.

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:59.450
When unconnected people come in,
they ought to abate temporarily.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:00.910
Really?

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:04.910
When TV psychic shows go to cover
famous haunted houses,

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:07.250
generally, nothing
ever happens, right?

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:09.920
Usually, the response gets weaker.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:12.590
The fact that it's getting stronger
instead means that something

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:13.920
is pushing back.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:15.880
You think so too, Monk?

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:20.590
Yeah. The house has realized that
we're here, and now it's angry.

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:24.270
What's more, if it's showing us
these bold moves right off the bat,

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:27.600
it means that this is no
run-of-the-mill poltergeist.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:30.600
We might have a hard time with this.

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:37.280
And so, Ayami-chan's room
and the living room

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:41.280
were declared off-limits until
Naru's investigation was complete.

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:46.290
Ayami-chan then stayed
in Noriko-san's room.

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:54.630
The next morning,

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:58.630
the vase that was in the drawing
room had not moved one bit.

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:01.680
Did that mean that this really
was the work of a spirit?

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:06.970
I reverently pray for thy presence.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:10.980
Deign to ensconce thyself
in this unhallowed place,

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:14.650
and purify its many vessels.

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:17.650
I ask that my humble
plea may be heard,

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:22.660
that peace and calm may be
granted unto this place.

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:26.660
The case is as good as solved now.

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:35.340
Naru, here's the check on
the temperatures in each room.

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:38.340
Ayami-chan's room
is a little lower, huh?

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:44.180
I'm told that in places where spirits
appear, the temperature drops.

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:48.680
There is no warping
or deformation to the house itself,

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:51.350
and the floors are pretty much flat.
There's also no sign

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:54.360
of any loss of subterranean water,
so it's not the ground sinking.

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:58.030
Does that mean the culprit
really is a spirit?

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:01.360
The possibility of that
is starting to increase.

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:02.700
You're serious?

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:05.370
What's that!?

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:10.700
Kana-san!

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:13.040
T-the flames just suddenly
started shooting up!

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:15.380
Please stand back.
Grab the extinguisher!

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:38.400
Huh?

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.400
Naru! Someone's there!

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:45.070
There's no one here.

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:47.490
There was!
Someone was looking inside!

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:48.830
A child...

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:06.050
Minnie, I'm going to tuck
you in now, okay?

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:17.440
Ayami...

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:21.780
Ayami, were you just looking
into the kitchen?

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:22.400
Uh-uh.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:25.450
But Mai-chan said she saw a child.

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:28.450
You really were peeking
in from out in the yard, right?

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:29.780
No I wasn't.

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:31.790
Ayami!

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:33.450
No!

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:36.210
It wasn't Ayami!!

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:37.920
W-what the-

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:41.800
It wasn't Ayami.

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:45.800
It wasn't!

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.130
Noriko-san!

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:51.470
Sissy!

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:52.810
Noriko-san!

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:07.820
You've botched things again,
haven't you?

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:10.490
I guess I just can't do anything.

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:14.830
Luckily, Noriko-san wasn't hurt.

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:18.170
That thing yesterday- what was it?

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:21.290
It appeared to react
to that little girl shouting.

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:23.840
It's possible that
it's tied in to the image

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:25.510
of the child you said you saw, Mai.

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:27.510
I believe Ayami-chan is the culprit.

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:31.850
I thought the suggestion experiment
proved that the culprit wasn't human.

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:34.180
How confident are you in the outcome?

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:36.520
100 percent.

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:39.190
Any possibility that
the suggestion failed?

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:39.600
None.

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:41.520
You're saying absolutely none?

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:42.860
Naru...

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:46.860
The temperature in Ayami-chan's
room is starting to drop.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:50.200
Lin, the speaker!

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.870
This is severe.

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:07.550
There's not even anyone
in Ayami-chan's room, either...

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:09.550
Incredible...

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:11.220
What?

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:12.890
The temperature.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:20.230
It's dropping with incredible force.
It's almost below freezing.

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:24.570
Are you saying that the culprit
behind the poltergeisting is...

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:26.900
It couldn't possibly be Ayami-chan.

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:30.240
No, this is not the work of humans.

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:37.330
Ayami-chan sure is well-behaved.

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:41.750
Up until just a while ago, she was
more cheerful, and friendly to others.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:43.580
She only got like this
after my brother remarried,

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:45.920
and they came to live in this house.

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:52.180
Ayami-chan, here's your snack.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.600
It's nice to have someone
to play with, huh?

00:15:57.600 --> 00:15:59.270
What are you doing?

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:04.940
I really wish you would answer me.
Here, have a cookie.

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:08.280
You don't want it?

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:14.950
I see.

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:16.620
Suit yourself, then!

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:24.290
Oh, Ayami...

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:27.630
If you don't want them,
then Sissy will eat them, okay?

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:28.630
No!

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:32.630
They're poisoned!

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:35.800
Minnie told me so.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:38.310
She said there's poison
in the snacks.

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:41.310
She said that woman is an evil witch.

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:43.640
She made Dad her
servant with her magic.

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:48.650
Ayami and Sissy are in the way,
so she's trying to kill us!

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:50.480
What was that?

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:57.660
Minnie told her so?

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:09.130
Huh?

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:17.010
This is the guest room
at Noriko-san's house...

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:22.020
Oh, yeah... I guess I came back
here earlier and fell asleep...

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:31.690
Naru? But why?

00:17:31.690 --> 00:17:34.030
W-what's wrong?

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:38.700
Huh? What?

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:45.710
Ayami-chan is in danger.

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:50.040
Huh? What... what do you mean?

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:53.050
What do you mean,
Ayami-chan is in danger?

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:58.050
Hey, Naru! In danger from what!?
What's going on!?

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:02.720
Naru!

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:14.740
Why...

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:22.080
Look at me! I-I'm dreaming
about Naru again!

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:24.660
And at a time like this!

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:29.420
Oh, yeah, I forgot.

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:32.090
Minnie told her so?

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:33.750
Ayami-chan said that?

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:36.880
Mm-hmm. Isn't that kind of eerie?

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:44.770
It was a dream, all right.
Seeing this guy smile like that...

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:46.770
This is Minnie, right here.

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:53.440
My brother bought it for her,
just before they moved into this house.

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:03.120
Did Ayami-chan's behavior
change before then? Or after?

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:05.450
After, I think.

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:11.790
Give her back!

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:13.790
Give Minnie back!

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:16.130
Don't touch her!

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:20.130
Ayami-chan, I understand
you're able to talk to Minnie.

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:30.020
Nobody is allowed to touch her!

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:31.650
Ayami!

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:07.510
I'm sorry, Ayami-chan.

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:10.180
I need to borrow Minnie
for a bit, okay?

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.540
So that's Minnie, huh?

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:38.000
I'm surprised the little tyke
let you borrow it.

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:41.380
We kind of took it after
Ayami-chan fell asleep.

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:45.550
It seems kind of creepy, huh?

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:47.220
I guess.

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:52.230
Dolls were originally meant as vessels
for trapping people's souls.

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:56.900
Without any soul, and being empty
on the inside, they're easy to possess.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:21:00.570
So, what exactly are you doing now?

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:02.400
Naru, what's the mat-

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:11.370
Minnie?

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:14.370
No way! She was sitting a minute ago!

00:23:43.400 --> 00:23:48.360
Next time: File 2,
"The Doll House" #2
